      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/3/40/1",
      "text": [
        ": سَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ اَلرَّجُلِ كَيْفَ يُنْكِحُ عَبْدَهُ أَمَتَهُ قَالَ \"يُجْزِيهِ أَنْ يَقُولَ قَدْ أَنْكَحْتُكَ فُلاَنَةَ وَ يُعْطِيهَا مَا شَاءَ مِنْ قِبَلِهِ أَوْ مِنْ قِبَلِ مَوْلاَهُ وَ لاَ بُدَّ مِنْ طَعَامٍ أَوْ دِرْهَمٍ أَوْ نَحْوِ ذَلِكَ وَ لاَ بَأْسَ بِأَنْ يَأْذَنَ لَهُ فَيَشْتَرِيَ مِنْ مَالِهِ إِنْ كَانَ لَهُ جَارِيَةً أَوْ جَوَارِيَ يَطَؤُهُنَّ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4553 - Al-Alaa narrated from Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Abu Jafar Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as), who said: I asked him how a man can marry his slave to his bondwoman.\nImam (as) said: \"It is sufficient for him to say, 'I have married you to so-and-so,' and to give her whatever he wishes, either from himself or from her master. There must be something given, whether it be food, a dirham, or something similar.\nThere is also no harm if he permits the slave to purchase a bondwoman from his own wealth, if he has any, to have relations with her.\""
        ]
      }
    },
